Zero-area cache entries (spaces, see lookup_or_rasterize_request) are stored with x = 0, so `self.x - ATLAS_PADDING` underflows u16 (panic in debug, wrap in release) when reached via the public debug_glyph. Return an empty rect for entries that own no texels:

pub fn allocation_rect(self) -> [u16; 4] {
    if self.width == 0 || self.height == 0 {
        return [0; 4];
    }
    [
        self.x - ATLAS_PADDING,
        self.y - ATLAS_PADDING,
        self.width + ATLAS_PADDING * 2,
        self.height + ATLAS_PADDING * 2,
    ]
}
